ars":2,"record":"6-4","score":-1.91,"index":2.39,"talentRank":65,"why":["year 2: prove-it window"]},{"id":"154","coach":"Jake Dickert","years":3,"record":"9-1","score":-2.24,"index":2.24,"talentRank":63,"why":["year 3: prove-it window"]}],"method":"CFB extras: Heisman tracker and coaching hot seat. Both are transparent heuristics, labeled as such.\n\nHeisman score (modeled on who actually wins: a big-stat QB, sometimes a skill player, on a top team):\n  production per game  QB: (pass yds + 20 x pass TD - 45 x INT + rush yds + 20 x rush TD) / games\n                       RB/WR/TE: (scrimmage yds + 20 x TD) / games x 0.85 (voters favor QBs)\n  team factor          x (1 + 0.6 x max(0, (30 - power rank) / 30)) x (0.7 + 0.3 x win %)\n  odds                 softmax over the field (temperature 90), so the board sums to 100%.\n  Players currently out (injury list / inactive) are dropped from contention.\n\nHot seat score: how far the team trails expectations (the disappointment index, flipped), scaled\nby tenure (year 1 is protected, years 2-5 are the danger zone), plus extra pressure when an elite-\ntalent roster is losing and when the team has a losing record. No buyout data is used: no free\nsource has it."}